<title>GERMANY: Pan-German Feb industry output rises 1.9 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>Pan-German Feb industry output rises 1.9 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The economics ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT  Feb 97     Jan 97	Feb 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)   +1.9	 -1.5	 -2.9</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +7.1	 +2.0	 -7.5</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)	     100.0	 98.1(97.9) 93.4</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional. The year-on-year figures are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank statistics.</p>
<p>The economics ministry added that even without a seasonal boost from the construction industry, industry output was up 0.5 percent in February.</p>
<p>&quot;Particularly the clear recovery in the manufacturing sector -- the core industry sector -- continued the clear upswing of the past few months,&quot; it said.</p>
